1
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for a certain day
that floats on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kick a pebble and my shoe flies off too,

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,200
onto the head of the
carpenter I was messing with.

4
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:55,280
Above all, even if you lose your spirit,
Katsushika is always here for you.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,560
With a yawn, nothing changes.
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:14,660
From the water tower with its pointed cap,
up into the big sky.

8
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,800
The sun sets.

9
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,360
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost again.

11
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

12
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:41,677
Really?

13
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:45,700
So that's what happened
while I was taking time off.

14
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:48,140
Well, it's pretty much the usual, though.

15
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:54,000
Senpai, is something wrong?

16
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,720
So this place is finally closing

17
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:05,400
Even in Tokyo, the second-
and third-run theaters have been disappearing one after another lately.

18
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,840
Ryo-chan,
is this a cinema you have memories of?

19
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:08,740
Well, yeah.

20
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:13,640
When I was a kid, movies were the king
of entertainment, no doubt about it.

21
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:17,100
Back then there were countless
movie theaters all over Japan,

22
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:22,920
but my most cherished memory
is definitely this Orion-za.

23
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:35,880
Asakusa Rokku, through the Meiji,
Taisho, and Showa eras,

24
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:40,560
the movie district that built Japan's era of moving pictures,
an entertainment district.

25
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:47,120
ever since the Denkikan opened as
Japan's first movie theater in Meiji 30,

26
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:51,580
countless theaters raised their curtains one after another,
like stars in the sky.

27
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:56,720
When I was a child,
movies entered their golden age.

28
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,380
In those days,
movies were truly the king of entertainment.

29
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:05,400
This is

30
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:09,440
a story of my memories
of Orion-za from that era.

31
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,220
Don't rush like that, this way!

32
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:18,940
It's already starting!

33
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:22,560
We made it!

34
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,180
The brakes won't work!

35
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,700
If we pay for the movie,
we can't buy ice cream inside, you know.

36
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,260
Let's use the usual trick.

37
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,740
Excuse me,
one elementary school ticket, please.

38
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:40,520
Yes.

39
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,320
Here you go.

40
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,860
Hey, wait a second.

41
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:54,200
Why are you making him
wear a coat in summer?

42
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,780
He has a cold.

43
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,840
Nakagawa, what is this guy?

44
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:00,700
Damn.

45
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,480
"Damn" isn't the point, is it?

46
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,960
There's no opening, no gap in my defense.

47
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:08,740
Now that I think about it,
there should be one more of them.

48
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:11,140
Where on earth?

49
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,780
In a place like that?

50
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:17,120
You're like a gecko, you!

51
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,820
What are you doing to a paying customer?

52
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:26,700
Skimming the admission fee,
what kind of customer are you?

53
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:30,180
Fine, I'll pay the money.

54
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,000
Cheapskate.

55
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,860
Of course.

56
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,660
Now we can't buy ice cream anymore.

57
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:37,920
Well, it's fine. I've got 700 yen to spare.

58
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,560
What, 700 yen?

59
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,060
Damn it.

60
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,060
It's nice and cool in here.

61
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,520
The air conditioning is only in here,
after all.

62
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:52,420
It's packed. Looks like standing room only.

63
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:56,900
Let's find an open seat.

64
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:58,840
You two, take the right side.

65
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,140
Got it.

66
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:00,520
Just as I thought, it's crowded.

67
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,020
There's nothing open at all.

68
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:02,860
Right.

69
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,360
Not even two are open.

70
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,080
How about over there?

71
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,020
No good, none are open.

72
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:09,440
Nothing we can do.

73
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:10,780
Let's watch from the very front.

74
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,560
It's easier to watch sitting down.

75
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:15,600
It's hard to see, but it has presence!

76
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:17,480
Probably.

77
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:23,000
I had no idea you loved movies so much,
Ryo-chan.

78
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,660
What?

79
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:34,500
There were no games, and plenty of homes didn't have TVs.
Every kid went to the movies back then. And when it came to movie theaters, above all,

80
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:40,760
it was breaking ramune bottles! What's that?
Ramune bottles have marbles inside, right?

81
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:49,760
You break the bottle to get it out. But why at the movie theater?
Well, it's always lively there, so the rolling bottles all gather up at the front.

82
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,520
You trap them like this with your feet, see.

83
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:59,180
Back then, whenever kids got bored of the movie,
they'd all play at breaking bottles.

84
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:02,000
You did that during the screening?

85
00:06:02,260 --> 00:06:06,700
Yeah. When adults scolded us, we'd stop for a bit,
but it would start up again right away.

86
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:09,980
So in the end, the cinema started
handing out prizes for them.

87
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,380
After that, it never stopped.

88
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:16,100
Then some clever criminals showed up, bringing
in bottles they'd picked up off the street.

89
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,340
You were the senior one in that, right?

90
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,160
Well, yeah.

91
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:23,300
Speaking of which, you said
earlier you had a most memorable one?

92
00:06:25,268 --> 00:06:29,160
it was one day during my childhood,
when I was lost in movies day and night.

93
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:32,780
My lord, please, have some restraint!

94
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,520
Come now, come now, what's the harm?

95
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,820
S-someone help!

96
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:40,160
No one will come.

97
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,040
Hang in there, my lord. Just a little more.

98
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:46,260
Kintaro the Samurai, has arrived.

99
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:46,940
What?

100
00:06:46,940 --> 00:07:06,840
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

101
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,460
Let go of me! Let go! This guy's the reason!

102
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,520
Why me!

103
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,320
What the hell are you doing!

104
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,420
Aaaaah!

105
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:15,320
Aaaaah!

106
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,880
Aaaaaaah!

107
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:17,560
Aaaaaaah!

108
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,220
Aaaaaaah!

109
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:18,860
Aaaaaaah!

110
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:19,160
Aaaaaaah!

111
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:19,400
Aaaaaaah!

112
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,140
Was it you two who did this!

113
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,700
Strong! So strong!

114
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,540
This way!

115
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,940
Three, four!

116
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,480
Six, seven!

117
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:36,940
Damn it! They're like rats!

118
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:58,220
This is all Kankichi's fault!

119
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:01,120
We paid our money and nearly got thrown out.

120
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,240
But still...

121
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,000
What are you doing, you lot?

122
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,880
This area is off-limits.

123
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,080
Sorry.

124
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,480
So it's you lot.

125
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:13,300
The ones who've been making a racket,
smashing bottles and climbing onto the stage,

126
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:17,220
I can't stand people who come to
a cinema and don't watch the movie.

127
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:19,080
Get out already.

128
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,760
What did you say?

129
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:22,860
What's wrong, Hikaru?

130
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:23,980
Dad.

131
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,780
Is that Kankichi-kun?

132
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:29,780
Tsukudani... you're Gin-san's kid, right?

133
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,620
How do you know my name?

134
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:35,180
You used to come see movies with Gin-san all the time when you were little,
didn't you?

135
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,500
I remember.

136
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:37,620
So, what do you think?

137
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,560
Want to take a look around?

138
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,080
Is that really okay?

139
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,220
You've never been in a projection booth before,
have you?

140
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,460
Dad.

141
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:45,480
Come on, don't be like that.

142
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:48,060
It's a movie projector room, isn't it!

143
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,440
So this is the projection booth.

144
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,760
Wow, this is amazing!

145
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,020
So this machine is what projects the film?

146
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:56,500
But it's hot in here

147
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,200
It's because the heat from
the projector lamps is intense.

148
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:02,460
They're venting the heat
through this carbon duct, but

149
00:09:02,460 --> 00:09:03,260
it's still hot.

150
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:06,000
In summer, it's basically a scorching hell.

151
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:09,580
Why are there two of the same machine?

152
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,620
It's so we can switch the film reels.

153
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:12,540
Switch them?

154
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:12,960
Yeah.

155
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,980
It should be almost time.

156
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:17,180
Look from here.

157
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,820
You can see the screen.

158
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,120
It's like a front-row seat.

159
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,100
Watch closely.

160
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,720
A mark is going to appear on
the right edge of the screen now.

161
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:26,800
It really is.

162
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:29,000
We switch on the second mark.

163
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,040
Now this side has moved.

164
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:35,280
So this is how it works.

165
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,120
Each reel is about 13 minutes, you know.

166
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,660
It's a film that runs an hour and a half,

167
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,360
so it's about seven reels.

168
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:42,720
Hey, Hikaru.

169
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,960
Keep this one running.

170
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:46,320
That's one whole movie's worth.

171
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,880
Don't touch it, okay?

172
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,840
Is he showing off?

173
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:53,260
But he's impressive, isn't he?
He's still in middle school, right?

174
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,820
He's still only half a man's worth.

175
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:59,600
We only have him helping with
the chores during summer vacation.

176
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:02,440
If you let me, I can do it too!

177
00:10:03,340 --> 00:10:04,260
That's right, isn't it.

178
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:09,900
It's slow.
The next reel should be arriving about now.

179
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,560
The next reel?

180
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,120
We share one film across several reels.

181
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,880
We stagger the screening times in turn,

182
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:20,920
and carry each finished
reel over to the next cinema.

183
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:23,880
Wow, if it doesn't arrive in time,
that would be a disaster.

184
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:28,380
Yeah, the audience would be left
waiting in the middle of the film.

185
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:32,200
Here it comes! I'll go grab the reel,
so you're in charge from here.

186
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:32,900
Yes.

187
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,660
The film's snapped!

188
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:41,400
Oh no, the lamp's -

189
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:44,540
What's wrong?

190
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:45,940
What are you doing?

191
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,440
The audience is starting to get restless!

192
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,440
Without knowing what
we're dealing with here,

193
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:52,120
we have to splice it quickly,

194
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,440
I'll do that later.

195
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:57,520
More importantly,
we can't keep the customers waiting.

196
00:10:59,580 --> 00:10:59,940
Right.

197
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:04,860
Okay, that's good.

198
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:10,880
Hey, are you all right?

199
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:13,460
This is nothing, I'm fine.

200
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:16,700
Good, it's just a background scene.

201
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:19,680
If it were a dialogue scene,
the conversation would skip, you know.

202
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,200
That's tough, doing all that.

203
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Not at all, I just love movies.

204
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:30,000
Movies are made with so much
work going on behind the scenes

205
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,140
that we never see,
with so many people struggling for them.

206
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,640
Yeah, it's a shame we just sit back and
watch like we have nothing to do with it.

207
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:43,580
Dad

208
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:47,580
Why did you let those guys
into the projection booth?

209
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:51,260
Those kids love movies in their own way.

210
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:56,460
Anyone who loves movies would want to peek
into the projection booth at least once.

211
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,040
But

212
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,620
That's strange.

213
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:05,660
The manager and the others should have gone home.
Is someone still here?

214
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:10,880
You two?

215
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:15,920
I was going to clean up the
bottles we made a mess of earlier.

216
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,860
Sorry for making all the noise, Hikaru-kun.

217
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,900
That's how we became
friends with Hikaru-kun.

218
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,660
Ever since then,

219
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:41,340
we practically lived at the Orion Theater.

220
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:43,680
So you went to the movies every day?

221
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:47,480
Of course, they let us in
for free through the back door.

222
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:52,100
I used to talk about movies
with Hikaru-kun almost every day.

223
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:56,280
I like Tokijiro of Kutsukake,
starring Raizo.

224
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:58,500
Kirare Yosaburo was good too.

225
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:00,800
Kankichi-kun,
you really know your period dramas.

226
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:05,020
I've been coming to the theater
with my father since I was a kid.

227
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:07,620
I came every day,
so I even memorized the lines.

228
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,780
So next week it's this one.

229
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:13,460
But the films change every week,
so it must be tough.

230
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,580
You have to remember the titles properly.

231
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,300
This thing is also
called the sewing machine.

232
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:22,160
See, its movement looks like a
sewing machine bobbing its needle.

233
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:22,940
It really does.

234
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:27,320
In the V-Room,
24 frames of picture flow past every second.

235
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:33,340
That's why the projector blinks 24
times a second while it shows the movie.

236
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,100
Wow.

237
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:45,180
I don't have a projectionist's license yet,
so all I can do is odd jobs,

238
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,260
but once I get my license
and join a film company,

239
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:51,260
becoming a director is my dream.

240
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:53,040
A film director?

241
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:58,000
Yeah. My films will be shown in
movie theaters all over Japan.

242
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,580
Wow, directors have to
be really smart, right?

243
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:05,540
Dad said even people who graduate
from good universities fail the exams.

244
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,920
A film director

245
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,060
Ready... action!

246
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:17,500
For someone like me, who usually just drifts through life,
that dream felt so big.

247
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,759
You know, we weren't that far apart in age,

248
00:14:19,809 --> 00:14:22,580
but Hikaru always seemed so grown-up to me.

249
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:27,140
Then, as summer vacation was drawing to a close,
something terrible happened.

250
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,100
What, pneumonia?

251
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:37,360
Yes, he suddenly ran a fever this morning,
so we had a doctor come see him, and...

252
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,320
That's a problem.
The first screening is about to start.

253
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:44,740
Well, even if we call in
someone from outside...

254
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:47,380
I'll do it instead.

255
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,040
You?

256
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:49,460
Yes.

257
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,060
But you're...

258
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:52,960
My father has already agreed.

259
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,780
He'll need absolute bed rest for a while,
you know.

260
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:59,600
Even for a pro, today is the opening day,

261
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,520
Dad, I'll do it in your place.

262
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:05,960
Idiot, you're not even fully qualified yet!

263
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:09,240
It's fine, Dad. Leave it to me.

264
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:15,040
There's no choice.
Until the backup projectionist arrives,

265
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:16,240
please handle Theater A.

266
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:17,040
Yes.

267
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:19,040
Anyway, let's try asking somewhere else.

268
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:20,060
Hikaru-kun.

269
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,500
We heard what happened.

270
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:24,280
We'll help too.

271
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:25,840
Thank you.

272
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:44,520
The seats are already full of customers.

273
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:49,120
It's almost time to start the screening.

274
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,140
Hikaru-kun.

275
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,900
Then, Kankichi-kun, ring the buzzer.

276
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:53,360
Okay.

277
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,020
This one, then.

278
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,940
Tonpei-kun, dim the lights.

279
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:03,640
Got it.

280
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:05,420
Dimming the lights.

281
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:05,840
I see.

282
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:10,760
Kankichi-kun was waiting
with the curtain open.

283
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:19,080
Gradually lower the
screen's brightness... and...

284
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,700
Lens is good.

285
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,260
Start!

286
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:40,060
Wow, we're actually showing a movie!

287
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:43,220
It's kind of moving, isn't it.

288
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:46,760
I hope it keeps going smoothly from here.

289
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:08,626
Kankichi! Stop watching the movie and

290
00:17:08,676 --> 00:17:10,980
help me rewind the film!

291
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:12,540
Ah

292
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:16,020
This is trouble...

293
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:18,380
Hikaru, what's wrong?

294
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,380
The next reel still hasn't arrived.

295
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:22,400
What? Is that the only one left?

296
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:25,712
Yeah...
even though everything's going so well,

297
00:17:25,762 --> 00:17:28,500
if the rest of the film doesn't come...

298
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:28,600
...

299
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,900
I'll go check partway.

300
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:39,720
Kankichi.

301
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:53,460
It's the usual order,
but it should've already left Ginryukan.

302
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,360
This is the last reel.

303
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,800
So the movie's going to
cut off at the best part?

304
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:16,820
What? Already twenty minutes ago?

305
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:19,740
From here to Orion-za,

306
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,000
it should only take about
five minutes by motorcycle.

307
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,660
What on earth is going on?

308
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,200
Where on earth did it go?

309
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:45,580
No way.

310
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:48,660
Are you okay?

311
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:50,720
Looks like your leg bone is broken.

312
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,300
The ambulance is here!

313
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,480
Mister!

314
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,540
I came all the way from the Orion Theater.

315
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,580
Where's the film?

316
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,760
Because everyone's waiting for it.

317
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,580
Mister, what about the film?

318
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:13,320
Please.

319
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,520
Leave it to me, mister.

320
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:21,820
Hey, what time is it now?

321
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:23,980
It's just past 10:05.

322
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,120
We can still make it.

323
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:32,260
About five more minutes

324
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,900
Move, move, move!

325
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:41,700
Excuse me! Excuse me!

326
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,340
I've got it! A shortcut!

327
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,060
Now it's the stairs!

328
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:22,520
!

329
00:20:22,520 --> 00:20:22,880
Ugh!

330
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,960
Hot-tttt!

331
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:27,460
Gah!

332
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:27,920
The film!

333
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,860
Whoaaaaaaaaaa!

334
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:33,760
Gwah!

335
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:34,780
Hey, you!

336
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:37,280
Wait up! Hold on!

337
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:42,820
W-we really don't have any time left!

338
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:50,240
Doromajin?

339
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,880
Damn it! We're out of time!

340
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,180
Aaaaaah!

341
00:20:54,180 --> 00:21:02,500


342
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:03,520
We have less than a minute!

343
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:06,520
What on earth is Kankichi doing?

344
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:09,300
The Doromajin is going to
end right at the good part!

345
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,440
Hikaru!

346
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,280
Doromajin!

347
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,480
Idiot, it's me!

348
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,460
Kankichi, the film?

349
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:21,520
Right here!

350
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:23,780
Hikaru, catch!

351
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,320
Kankichi, thank you!

352
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,280
Ugh!

353
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:37,360
Aaaaaah, I'm dying!

354
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,340
Aaaaaah!

355
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,740
Eeeeeeeh!

356
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,520
We made it!

357
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:20,340
After that, projectors were automated and
the projectionist license was abolished too.

358
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:24,620
I haven't seen Hikaru at all since then.

359
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:28,220
What happened to Hikaru after that?

360
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:32,680
He became a director. Apparently he's
still working hard in the film world.

361
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:35,020
Well then, senpai, shall we go?

362
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,060
Where to?

363
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:39,520
Where to?
The last screening at Orion-za, of course.

364
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:40,260
Ryo-chan.

365
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:42,820
Right.

366
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:56,320
Thank you all for gathering today for the
final screening at our Orion-za theater,

367
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,980
we truly appreciate it.

368
00:22:58,860 --> 00:23:01,400
The films we are showing today

369
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:05,780
are all nostalgic
classics chosen by request.

370
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:09,300
Please relax and enjoy
the show until the very end.

371
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,640
I just love movies, you know.

372
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:23,680
Make a fuss, blend it together,
settle it quickly, cut it clean.

373
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:33,920
decided, a flash of inspiration, bouncing
along, gathering it all, taking action.

374
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:40,060
flying off, the most amazing power of all.

375
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:52,340
Everyone gather here,
the dreamlike final energy.

376
00:24:53,400 --> 00:25:03,480
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, painting the universe, standing on the earth,
the star of Kameari spun around in a circle.

377
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:08,700
That'll do, right? Like hell it will!

378
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:27,680
It's alive? And now you want me
to take it to the Dragon Palace?

379
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:31,606
Hold on, old man. I'm not a real turtle, and

380
00:25:31,656 --> 00:25:34,040
how the hell would I know
where the Dragon Palace is?

381
00:25:34,620 --> 00:25:37,540
Next time:
"The Turtle's Repayment." See you then.

